Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.88,0:00:12.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How long are we \Ngoing to stay here?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.22,0:00:14.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought we were \Ngoing to the border.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.51,0:00:15.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How should I know?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.04,0:00:20.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There will probably be many soldiers who will be confused and won't follow orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.34,0:00:22.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It will mean some sporadic fighting,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.78,0:00:25.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but we will keep the casualties to a minimum.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.99,0:00:46.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We are now going to \Nreturn to Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.91,0:00:51.28,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,With the troops we have at present, we will \Ntake control of the Central Command Center.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.72,0:00:53.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're planning to \Nstage a revolt?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.89,0:00:55.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'd rebel against the Führer?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.22,0:00:59.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer and those around him have used the country for their own purposes
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.69,0:01:02.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and led us down the wrong path!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.39,0:01:04.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll take control of the Assembly at the same time.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.83,0:01:08.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But this is all so sudden, \Nand without any evidence...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.39,0:01:09.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Evidence?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.74,0:01:12.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here is your evidence!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.28,0:01:16.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There isn't a single flaw in this well-trained body of mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.05,0:01:18.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This{\i0} is my evidence \Nthat my words are true!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.80,0:01:22.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go on, go on, look at it! \NTouch it! See for yourself!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.52,0:01:24.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go on, go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.27,0:01:25.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go on!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.37,0:01:28.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.42,0:01:34.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who obtain it are set free from the Law of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.99,0:01:38.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no need to pay a price \Nin order to obtain something, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.94,0:01:43.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We sought it and found it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.36,0:03:31.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.50,0:03:36.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I restructured your water into ethanol.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.11,0:03:39.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It vaporizes at room temperature.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.12,0:03:56.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well done...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.93,0:04:10.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Make sure you tidy up when you're finished...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.92,0:04:52.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed, Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.82,0:04:58.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.05,0:05:01.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's wrong? Did something happen in the village?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.89,0:05:05.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I came because I was concerned.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.26,0:05:06.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You finally took care of her, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.18,0:05:10.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not her...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.22,0:05:13.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, you're the one I really love!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.35,0:05:22.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is where it ends.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.09,0:05:24.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's no use. \NI'm the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.96,0:05:27.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So I hear.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.50,0:05:29.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well then, shall we try this out?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.73,0:05:31.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you've become \Nthe Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.45,0:05:34.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then you should still be perfectly fine \Nif I destroy this here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.77,0:05:37.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop! Don't you touch Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.50,0:05:43.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't have to worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.60,0:05:46.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm just going to carry him to you-know-who's place.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.32,0:05:48.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"You-know-who"?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.02,0:05:53.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The one Lust was talking about? The one who controls you
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.03,0:05:57.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and for whom you're seeking the Philosopher's Stone to make immortal?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.62,0:05:59.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe so,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.49,0:06:02.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,although it's not as though you have absolutely nothing to do with that person.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.17,0:06:07.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By any chance, \Nis the person above you
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.88,0:06:10.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the one who deliberately \Nenticed our mom
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.43,0:06:12.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and did those things to her?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.14,0:06:15.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It couldn't be! There's no way Dad would do those things!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.55,0:06:17.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.40,0:06:24.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, you've got the wrong guy! \NGo slow {\i1}him{\i0} down!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.61,0:06:26.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That guy can do anything, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.08,0:06:30.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not allowed to touch him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.57,0:06:34.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can use him to bring Mama back! \NIsn't that right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.83,0:06:36.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Enough already!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.08,0:06:41.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.75,0:06:45.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is your fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.04,0:06:48.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's your fault that Mama is gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.82,0:06:50.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.89,0:06:53.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama's gone! \NMama's gone! Mama's gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.68,0:06:55.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She was your mama too!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.73,0:07:02.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.93,0:07:09.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't have anything \Nto do with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.47,0:07:13.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm the one you want to kill.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.54,0:07:15.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not my mama!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.28,0:07:18.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've got nothing to do with you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.16,0:07:20.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sensei!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.45,0:07:32.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.07,0:07:35.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He cried.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.58,0:07:38.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I couldn't bring myself to cry.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.65,0:07:41.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, he did.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.33,0:07:45.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's as if he was doing it \Non my behalf.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.33,0:07:53.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've had enough. \NRight now, it's about Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.92,0:07:56.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I should be of some help, \Nsuch that I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.38,0:07:58.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why I'm here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.41,0:08:11.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, we need to get going.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.72,0:08:14.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on, hold on! \NThat's Central for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.51,0:08:16.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are lots of books here I've never even seen!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.16,0:08:19.39,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,They've even got this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.39,0:08:21.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't wait to see Ed and Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.39,0:08:21.56,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,And this too!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.72,0:08:25.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you have enough?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.64,0:08:29.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Uh-oh, if I pick these up, we won't be able to afford a room tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.26,0:08:32.46,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,{\i1}But if I don't get them now, there's no telling when I can get them again.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.46,0:08:33.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On my tab?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.20,0:08:34.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.80,0:08:39.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This shop specializes in books for our regular customers, the State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.32,0:08:42.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You couldn't understand \Nwhat you'd read in these anyhow.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.30,0:08:46.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On... On my State Alchemist's tab.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.04,0:08:49.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To tell you the truth...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.78,0:08:57.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.99,0:08:59.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this him? Edward Elric?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.80,0:09:03.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, he definitely identified himself as the Fullmetal Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.46,0:09:07.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,W-Wait a minute! I was just joking around! I'm really—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.09,0:09:08.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell us all about it at \Nthe Command Center.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.73,0:09:11.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are orders to place you in custody as soon as you're found.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.63,0:09:12.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, what's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.31,0:09:14.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Keep back, Fletcher!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.24,0:09:16.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's his brother! \NThe younger Elric brother is here!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.43,0:09:18.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold it! Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.28,0:09:19.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't struggle!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.24,0:09:20.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.26,0:09:22.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Was the younger brother the shorter one?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.03,0:09:23.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, of course he is!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.75,0:09:27.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What did you do, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.16,0:09:29.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Central is a scary place.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.64,0:09:38.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.93,0:09:41.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You sealed the homunculus?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.82,0:09:43.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It wasn't me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.12,0:09:45.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was probably...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.07,0:09:49.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In any case, that means \Nthere are four of them left:
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.05,0:09:54.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the child, the one who eats everything, \Nthe one who can transform into anything,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.05,0:09:55.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the Führer.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.53,0:09:59.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And the one who's above them.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.34,0:10:02.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who's there?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.70,0:10:06.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nina, say hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.30,0:10:10.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter? \NAre you bashful? I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.16,0:10:15.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Her soul didn't come back, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.07,0:10:18.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nina, shall we play?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.44,0:10:20.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know! Where's Alexander?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.85,0:10:22.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where did Alexander go?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.90,0:10:25.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are we going to do with him? \NRight, Nina?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.53,0:10:26.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.78,0:10:29.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's a soulless doll.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.00,0:10:31.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is the form \Nhis sin has taken on.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.45,0:10:35.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's going to go on living, \Nembracing that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.27,0:10:36.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's good enough for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.62,0:10:43.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've grown up, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.18,0:10:45.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Grown up?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.73,0:10:52.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was sure I grew up when I decided to become a State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.21,0:10:58.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well then, what are \Nyou going to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.82,0:11:03.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I only know where one of \Nthe remaining homunculi is.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.01,0:11:07.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer, King Bradley.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.63,0:11:19.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?! \NHurry it up!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.83,0:11:29.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're completely surrounded.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.52,0:11:31.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There were even fewer soldiers \Nwho followed us than we expected.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.83,0:11:36.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing we can do about that. \NThe Führer's authority is absolute.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.24,0:11:38.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There aren't many officers who would go against it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.34,0:11:42.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, our new Brigadier General's plan was faulty.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.21,0:11:46.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, Mustang's plan \Nwas to buy time here
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.06,0:11:48.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and get Central's soldiers \Nto head this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.74,0:11:50.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now, we just have to hang in there for a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.32,0:11:51.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maj—Lt. Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.16,0:11:56.32,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Are you sure about me presuming to act like this, when I'm not even Brigadier General Mustang?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.32,0:11:59.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Keep your chin up. \NI am here with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.57,0:12:00.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.05,0:12:02.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it looks good on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.07,0:12:10.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, you can't, Lieutenant Havoc...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.19,0:12:15.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can I get you to keep \Nyour mouth closed?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.25,0:12:19.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. This must be some important work you're doing, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.14,0:12:24.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a top-secret mission. Make sure you don't mention it to anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.86,0:12:26.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.99,0:12:28.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not at all...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.18,0:12:30.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you angry about?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.71,0:12:32.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not angry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.34,0:12:38.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like Havoc and the others succeeded in making their move.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.55,0:12:39.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.78,0:12:42.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hurry, hurry, hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.91,0:12:46.65,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Our whole force has to catch up to \NBrigadier General Mustang's division tonight!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.48,0:12:52.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Impressive, being able to organize your division as quickly as that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.65,0:12:55.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I owe it all to your orders, Führer.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.57,0:12:58.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To think that you supposed that \Nsuch a circumstance as this would arise!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.93,0:13:01.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is now established that if Mustang and Armstrong are given some military force,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.60,0:13:03.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they are sure to launch a revolt,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.94,0:13:09.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,which makes them agitators, \Nthe same as Basque Grand was.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.06,0:13:13.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I had to promote him to Brigadier General \Nto make it look like I trusted him.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.24,0:13:16.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You men must have been \Nquite discontent about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.39,0:13:21.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course not! We will put them down and return within a day or two!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.56,0:13:29.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can I go home for the day?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.31,0:13:34.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, some boys using the name of the \NElric brothers were arrested this morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.88,0:13:36.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm, let's see...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.21,0:13:38.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dispose of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.00,0:13:42.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why did you say \Nyou were Edward Elric?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.77,0:13:45.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What was I supposed to do? We don't have any money.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.61,0:13:51.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We have to give them \Nthis journal page from Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.82,0:13:55.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hide it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.04,0:14:12.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks so much for doing this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.04,0:14:15.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, when it comes to \NHis Excellency's residence,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.09,0:14:17.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I had them put an \Nextreme rush on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.55,0:14:19.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, this is how the construction was completed?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.86,0:14:22.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I don't do sloppy work.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.28,0:14:27.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, it was laid out really weird. Usually, a wine cave is...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.06,0:14:30.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't quite understand it myself,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.07,0:14:32.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but those were the Führer's secretary's instructions.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.56,0:14:35.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The secretary is on leave, \Nso I am serving in her place.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.40,0:14:41.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Since you rushed to make the alterations, there's a little something extra in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.70,0:14:42.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, there is, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.14,0:14:46.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Command Center \Nsure is generous, all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.17,0:14:53.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The construction went according to schedule.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.90,0:14:56.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't say it's reliable, \Nbut this has to happen today.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.44,0:14:59.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.82,0:15:03.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a rumor that the Elric brothers \Nwere arrested this morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.28,0:15:13.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At least find out if the Führer is \Nhere or not beforehand, would you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.68,0:15:15.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What could I do?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.17,0:15:18.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who knew he was going home early for his kid's birthday?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.74,0:15:19.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There they are!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.44,0:15:20.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't make excuses!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.62,0:15:21.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Listen to reason!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.53,0:15:31.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn! Where did they go?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.53,0:15:32.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yow!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.90,0:15:34.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A-Are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.05,0:15:38.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys... The impostors?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.70,0:15:40.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Russell Tringham!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.29,0:15:43.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They were mistaken for you guys \Nand got arrested.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.29,0:15:46.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a troublesome tale, what with \Nthis much difference in our heights.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.96,0:15:49.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What was that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.73,0:15:49.43,Dialogue Alt,,20,20,0,,Huh? Have you gotten even shorter than before?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.43,0:15:51.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What did you say?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.43,0:15:51.71,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,B-Brother, that was uncalled for!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.71,0:15:52.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be quiet, Fletcher.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.76,0:15:56.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer suddenly \Nordered them to be executed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.38,0:15:58.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We thought that was too much,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.04,0:16:00.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and when we came to ask them what the situation was...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.17,0:16:03.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The commotion we caused allowed them to escape?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.97,0:16:04.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are they there?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.99,0:16:06.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Find them at once!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.98,0:16:10.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We finally meet again, \Nand here we have to leave right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.14,0:16:13.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where to?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.59,0:16:15.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer's residence, perhaps?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.51,0:16:19.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If that's the only place left...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.24,0:16:20.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,U-Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.84,0:16:21.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.26,0:16:24.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's part of our dad's journal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.08,0:16:26.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It has something from when \Nhe was in Central written on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.58,0:16:34.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sensei!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.78,0:16:37.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.82,0:16:50.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.44,0:16:54.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Frank...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.10,0:16:56.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Archer.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.95,0:16:58.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward Elric...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.75,0:17:02.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,as well as the woman who got away \Nfrom the Southern Command Center...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.66,0:17:14.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll take care of this. \NGo where it says in his journal.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.79,0:17:16.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sensei...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.02,0:17:18.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let me do something a teacher would do and get going!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.41,0:17:22.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys, too! Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.00,0:17:38.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,From the looks of it, you didn't \Nhave to help out here after all, Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.89,0:17:42.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You think they're the sort who would just quietly stay captured?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.03,0:17:43.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We know better than that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.65,0:17:44.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.08,0:17:51.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry, but I need your car—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.78,0:17:53.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fullmetal?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.17,0:17:55.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.55,0:17:57.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you're here \Nto capture me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.71,0:18:06.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, where are you going, Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.77,0:18:08.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Wague District.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.04,0:18:10.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer has a residence there.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.80,0:18:12.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What business do you have with the Führer?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.94,0:18:20.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess I don't have to ask. \NStill, it must be under guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.02,0:18:23.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major Armstrong is staging a rebellion for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.49,0:18:27.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I doubt they would even think I was in hiding in Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.33,0:18:29.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You were going to \Ndistinguish yourself in battle
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.51,0:18:31.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to rise to Führer, weren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.91,0:18:37.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You also became a dog of the military \Nin order to attain your goal. But then—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.17,0:18:38.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.16,0:18:44.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just swallow all of the evil that \Ncomes at you and realize your dream—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.41,0:18:47.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that's what I thought \Nthe right way to do things was.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.48,0:18:51.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you directly fight the Führer now, \Nyou won't be in the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.31,0:18:56.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if you do beat him, \Nyou'll never be able to be a leader again.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.01,0:18:57.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The masses won't acknowledge you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.57,0:19:03.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so, I can't let that man \Nget away with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.92,0:19:06.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going to avenge \NLieutenant Colonel Hughes, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.78,0:19:11.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. He must have known everything that was going on within the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.44,0:19:16.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going to throw away everything you've obtained up to now for this?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.10,0:19:17.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No great loss.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.82,0:19:19.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Isn't that true for you too?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.44,0:19:22.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You gave up being a dog of the military for your brother's sake.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.12,0:19:26.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You spat up the evil you've swallowed, trying to pretend you're an adult.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.32,0:19:31.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Both of us are trying like little children to be faithful in living out our dreams.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.92,0:19:35.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're coming with me, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.26,0:19:42.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I tried working for the military, \Nbut I thought that wars are something
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.41,0:19:45.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that somebody somewhere started \Nand ended in some place unknown to us,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.68,0:19:49.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that we didn't have \Nanything to do with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.83,0:19:51.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.19,0:19:55.48,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,there's someone out there who manipulates wars to make Philosopher's Stones.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.48,0:19:58.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So as long as there are people \Nwho seek the Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.53,0:20:00.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the wars will continue.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.72,0:20:04.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And the inclination to wage them \Nis within all of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.47,0:20:07.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The homunculi fan the flames of war.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.81,0:20:10.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But it's human transmutation that creates them.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.41,0:20:16.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're nothing more than what \Nour hearts and wits made them to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.52,0:20:18.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And if that's the case,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.08,0:20:21.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then there's no such thing as a war we don't have anything to do with.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.39,0:20:25.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But that is too much \Nfor us to take on.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.57,0:20:30.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All you and I can do at any one time \Nis what is before us.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.53,0:20:37.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to find this \N"you-know-who" person and defeat them.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.39,0:20:40.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then I'm going to destroy the Philosopher's Stone
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.74,0:20:43.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so that nobody will ever remember it again...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.85,0:20:46.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so that it will vanish from everyone's memories.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.18,0:20:47.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Destroy it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.49,0:20:50.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone? \NThen you really did complete it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.88,0:20:52.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, does that mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.62,0:20:55.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's not the one who brought about \Nthe Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.71,0:20:57.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was our hearts.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.03,0:20:59.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But that was your dream, wasn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.95,0:21:02.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To use the Philosopher's Stone \Nto take back what you had lost?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.37,0:21:07.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It won't help anything if it's just our dreams that come true.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.54,0:21:13.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's something more important than your dreams, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.09,0:21:15.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There always is.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.93,0:21:19.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something more important \Nthan ourselves, or our dreams...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.55,0:21:43.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Farewell.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.43,0:21:45.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good-bye.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.54,0:23:40.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.35,0:23:43.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 49: "The Other Side of the Gate"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.27,0:23:47.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On September 2nd, AD 1916,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.40,0:23:52.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,fourteen devils shrouded the skies over London.
